      "threadSnapshot": {
        "title": "fix: count tangled.create-repo jobs in the dashboard aggregation",
        "body": "The per-repo job aggregation filtered on the three `github.*` ref kinds,\nomitting `tangled.create-repo` -- the kind enrollment and resync actually\nenqueue. A create-repo job that was retrying or sitting at `failed` could\ntherefore never move a repo to `behind` or `error`.\n\nOne line plus a comment in `dashboard.get.ts`. The kind already carries\nthe same `installationId`/`githubRepoId` payload shape, so the existing\ngrouping is unchanged. No dependency on any other fix.\n\nTests: full unit suite passes. No tests added: the change is a kind\nstring inside the raw `sql` filter in the `dashboard.get.ts` route\nhandler, and no route handler in this repo has unit coverage -- the suite\ntargets utils and pure functions. The consumer of that query's output,\n`repoHealth()`, is already covered directly."
      },
      "source": "poll"
    },
